title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › Payment checks: authorization to other insurance
route: /authorizations/eligibility/R-1042
intro: Rows 4 to 7 of 'Payment checks' (the closed section on the result page), then, where this list is shown in the New case drawer, a last line about what the patient pays. On the result page the cost share is under Benefits in the summary instead. Authorization is the only row that can turn the verdict amber. The others turn it red.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: 'Limit reached' has a seeded patient (R-0921) and 'Another plan pays first' has one (I-2275). Both have a chip under 'Try a sample' on Verify.
---
start s1 "Result page, section 'Payment checks' opened, rows 4 to 7"
decision q9 "Was coverage found?"
endx x9 "Coverage not found\nRows 2 to 7 and any cost line are not shown\nOne grey row says nothing else could be checked"

group gA "Row 4 · Authorization"
  decision a0 "What is the authorization state?"
  process a1 "Chip 'Not required' (green)\n'Beacon does not require one for IOP.'"
  process a2 "Chip 'On file' (green)\n'On file with Summit. 9 of 14 days used'"
  process a3 "Chip 'Required' (amber)\n'Required before the first day. Not on file yet. A request is being drafted'"
  process a4 "Chip 'Under review' (amber)\n'Required. A request is with Cardinal and under review'"
  process a5 "Chip 'Retro request open' (amber)\n'A retro-authorization request is open. It covers days already delivered'"
  process a6 "Chip 'Required' (amber)\n'Required before the first day. Not on file yet. Start an authorization'"
endgroup

group gB "Row 5 · Can the clinic bill?"
  decision b0 "Is the clinic enrolled with this payer for this level of care?"
  process b1 "Title 'The clinic can bill', chip 'In network' (green)\n'The clinic is enrolled and in network with Summit for residential 3.5'"
  process b2 "Title 'The clinic cannot bill yet', chip 'Not enrolled' (red)\n'Claims would be rejected. Navigator can start the enrollment.'"
endgroup

group gC "Row 6 · Limits"
  decision c0 "Is there a day or unit limit?"
  process c1 "Chip '5 days left' (green), or amber at 3 or fewer\n'9 of 14 days used in this authorization period'"
  process c2 "Title 'Every authorized day is used' (or unit)\nChip 'Limit reached' (red)\n'14 of 14 days used in this authorization period. Nothing is left. Ask Cardinal for more days before the next day of service'"
  process c3 "Chip 'No limit' (green)\n'No annual day limit for residential care. The authorization sets the days'\nor 'No visit or day limit applies to this program'"
endgroup

group gD "Row 7 · Other insurance"
  decision d0 "Did the check find another plan?"
  process d1 "Title 'No other insurance', chip 'None' (green)\n'None found. Medicaid pays last, so we checked for another payer'"
  process d2 "Title 'Another plan pays first', chip 'Other plan' (red)\n'A second plan was found. It must be billed before this one.'"
endgroup

group gP "Last line (New case drawer only; the result page shows it under Benefits)"
  decision p0 "Does the plan type have a cost share on file?"
  process p1 "'What the patient pays:'\nHarborview 'Deductible $85 left, coinsurance 20%.'\nBeacon and Lakeshore 'Copay $40 per day, deductible $350 left, coinsurance 20% after the deductible.'"
  toast p2 "'This does not change what the clinic is paid.'"
  process p3 "Ohio Medicaid: no line at all\nNo '$0 copay' text, because members usually pay none"
endgroup

goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Medical records › Patient and insurance rows"
s1 --> q9
q9 -->|No| x9
q9 -->|Yes| a0
a0 -->|Not required| a1 --> b0
a0 -->|On file| a2 --> b0
a0 -->|Being drafted| a3 --> b0
a0 -->|With the payer| a4 --> b0
a0 -->|Retro request| a5 --> b0
a0 -->|Required, not started| a6 --> b0
b0 -->|Yes| b1 --> c0
b0 -->|No| b2 --> c0
c0 -->|Limit, room left| c1 --> d0
c0 -->|Limit, none left| c2 --> d0
c0 -->|No limit| c3 --> d0
d0 -->|No| d1 --> p0
d0 -->|Yes| d2 --> p0
p0 -->|Yes| p1 --> p2 --> g1
p0 -->|No| p3 --> g1
